Working Principle — NeerRakshak

1. Leakage Detection

A water leakage sensor detects the presence of water in the monitored area.

2. Signal Processing

The ESP32 reads the sensor output and determines whether the detected condition meets the configured leakage threshold.

3. Alert System

When leakage is detected, the ESP32 activates the planned alert mechanism to notify the user.

4. Automatic Water Shut-Off

The controller activates a suitable switching or actuator mechanism to close the water valve, once the final hardware design is confirmed.

5. System Reset

After the leak is resolved, the system can be checked and reset according to the implemented control logic.

Current Development Status

The system design is being documented. Hardware assembly and testing have not started yet.
